IMPORT prelude

-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1998 (Tas) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR, FLOOR,
-- MODULO), not the daydate library. The Act counts its periods in months ("within 12 months after", s 63(1); "within 6
-- months after notification", s 78(2)) and in days ("within 42 days after its receipt", s 64(2); "within 28 days after",
-- ss 59(2)-(4), 65(3), 71(4), 93(2), 100(2)).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website (State of Tasmania, CC BY 4.0); not the
-- authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Anti-Discrimination Act 1998`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- "Within n days after" day D: the day of D excluded, so the last day is D plus n (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The same day of the month n months later; a day the later month does not have falls on its last day (31 August plus
-- 6 months is 28 or 29 February). "Within 12 months after" day D is read as ending at the end of this day with n = 12
-- (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the days in month` `the target month` `of` `the target year`)) `the target month` `the target year`
    WHERE
        `the month index` MEANS DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1 PLUS n
        `the target year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS FLOOR (`the month index` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the target month` MEANS (`the month index` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
